## Langfuse’s Slack app reaches workspaces restricted to Marketplace apps

Source: Langfuse — https://langfuse.com/changelog/2026-10-30-slack-marketplace
Published: 2026-10-30
Channel: news

Langfuse records and evaluates AI application activity. Its Slack app is now listed in the Slack Marketplace, allowing installation in workspaces that permit only Marketplace apps. The change helps teams bring existing observability notifications into their working channels.

A Workspace Owner can pre-approve the app where approval is required. Teams then connect Slack in the project’s integration settings and route prompt-change notifications or alerts on latency, cost and scores to appropriate channels. The announcement concerns availability and setup; it does not claim new alert-detection logic.

Why it matters: For teams blocked by Slack app restrictions: check Marketplace approval, then configure the project integration and relevant notification channels.

